{
  "cafeSelector": [
    {
      "text": "The first item in a to-do list is always the hardest one to cross off."
    },
    {
      "text": "If we could just get one item done, the rest would surely follow. We just need to start."
    },
    {
      "text": "That's why some people find the easiest item first, and start from there."
    },
    {
      "text": "It gives them a better chance at getting something done."
    },
    {
      "text": "This is because setting things in motion is difficult."
    },
    {
      "text": "Choosing to do homework is difficult. Choosing to clean your room is difficult. Choosing to get out of bed is difficult."
    },
    {
      "text": "Change is uncomfortable. It's always easier to leave things the way they are. To let the flow carry you."
    },
    {
      "text": "Until you reach a point where doing nothing does more damage than doing anything."
    },
    {
      "text": "When this happens, change is no longer a choice. It's a consequence."
    },
    {
      "text": "Is that also a choice? The choice to do nothing?"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lacie",
      "text": "...For now, I'll focus on getting the first item on the list done."
